<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>MISO Terminal: third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1a1a1a; background: #fff; }
  h1, h2, h3 { line-height: 1.2; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; }
  ul.crates { columns: 2 16rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #e6e6e6; background: #111; }
    pre { background: #1d1d1d; }
    a { color: #7fb4ff; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>MISO Terminal is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later (see <code>LICENSE</code>). It is built with the open-source
Rust crates below, whose licences ask that their notices travel with the
program. The licences of the fonts the terminal bundles are in the
<code>licenses</code> folder beside this file.</p>

<h2>Licences used</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>The licences, and the crates under each</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<section id="{{id}}">
  <h3>{{name}}</h3>
  <ul class="crates">
  {{#each used_by}}
    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
  {{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
